/br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can do that. What else is on the menu?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: There's ham, tofu turkey, plenty of vegetables, and cranberry sauce to start. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Tofu turkey?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Let's see if Peter knows the difference."}, {"time": "52000", "image": "engenn6le18ob01re2img09.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: This is ready. What now?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Add 2 teaspoons of vanilla. Sprinkle it with \u00bd teaspoon of nutmeg and a pinch or two of cinnamon. Cover it and put it in the fridge.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Wow! I'm cooking!"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Celebrating Christmas"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Christmas Traditions"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantities and Measures"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you cook, you use measures. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There's one for each of us. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I put in a lot of ginger."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Beat half a dozen eggs in this bowl."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use measures to talk about a specific amount when cooking. The measures can be international, in grams and kilos, or American measures, in teaspoons, cups and quarts.</p> You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item. Quantifiers do not indicate a specific quantity but rather a general amount."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Measurements\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a cup</br> a pinch / a dash</br> a teaspoon </p> a tablespoon </p> half a dozen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\".23 liters</br> a very small amount</br> 5 ml; a small measuring</br> spoon</br> 15 ml; a large measuring spoon</br> 6\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a/an/one</br> some</br> plenty of</br> a lot of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a single item</br> a general amount</br> more than is needed</br> a large amount\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Imperative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Imperative to give instructions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Beat half a dozen eggs in this bowl. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Add 3 cups milk and 8 tablespoons sugar. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Then put it on the burner and heat it very slowly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Imperative only has one form.</br>  The Imperative does not use a subject. </br> The subject, <span class=\"italic\">You</span>, is understood.</br> You often use the Imperative when you cook."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "savory"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "salty or spicy; not sweet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've cooked some savory dishes. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about cooking at Christmas."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cook up a storm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cook with great energy and skill"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She's really cooked up a storm for the event!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mixer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small appliance used to beat or whip food "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Use the mixer to beat the eggs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sharp or strong taste "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The gingerbread has a bite to it! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gingerbread"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cookie that contains ginger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You made gingerbread houses! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eggnog"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a traditional Christmas drink made with eggs, cream and spices "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can whip up the traditional eggnog! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tofu"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a high protein food made from soybeans "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a tofu turkey? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nutmeg"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a brown spice from a nut "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sprinkle some nutmeg on the eggnog. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cinnamon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a spice made from the bark of a tree "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like cinnamon in my eggnog too!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob01aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le18ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look up Christmas Recipes or Holiday Foods online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find 1 savory item and 1 sweet item that look appealing to you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Print out the pictures or do a little diagram of them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what the food is and what goes into it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your description to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do they think the food is appealing as well?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask them why or why not."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look up holiday foods."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about 1 savory and 1 sweet item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my description aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask my partner about how appealing the food is to them. "}]}]}